1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:03,519
Which plan still feeds people when a vehicle fails?

2
00:00:03,769 --> 00:00:09,017
FORK lets a coordinator test that decision before dispatch, with a synthetic mission.

3
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:16,419
This food bank has two hundred forty meals, two hundred sixty four requested, and three vehicles.

4
00:00:16,669 --> 00:00:20,776
Each strategy gets the same resources in an isolated world.

5
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:28,441
Velocity, Resilience, and Equity express different priorities in a deterministic planner.

6
00:00:28,691 --> 00:00:36,882
Ordinary greedy routing delivers two hundred twenty four meals initially, beating every named policy. FORK keeps that loss visible.

7
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:42,013
Now vehicle A fails at minute twenty five in every world.

8
00:00:42,263 --> 00:00:49,407
Completed deliveries stay completed. Its cargo stays stranded. Recovery can change only the remaining plan.

9
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:55,883
All three adapted plans now deliver one hundred sixty eight meals.

10
00:00:56,133 --> 00:01:06,351
With fixed routes under the same failure, they deliver one hundred forty four, one hundred twenty, and one hundred forty four. This measures recovery against a paired control.

11
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:14,222
Better depends on your priorities. Adjust coverage, high need service, and modeled cost.

12
00:01:14,472 --> 00:01:20,156
The comparison uses verified outcomes and reports ties instead of inventing a winner.

13
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:27,451
A separate referee reconstructs movement, cargo, and timing, then recomputes the metrics.

14
00:01:27,701 --> 00:01:31,379
Its receipt checks consistency inside the declared model.

15
00:01:31,629 --> 00:01:35,247
It does not prove route optimality or real world safety.

16
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:40,117
A person reviews the evidence and approves this revision.

17
00:01:40,367 --> 00:01:44,677
The exported packet carries the simulated plan and verification.

18
00:01:44,927 --> 00:01:51,278
Nothing is dispatched. FORK makes tradeoffs inspectable, and leaves the decision with the coordinator.
